 ],
 "says": "A person whose bound repository already holds a committed knowledge source (repository.bind, source.home.register, source.revision.commit) imports an external package of tax guidance into their own scope through the import_external_package route (source.revision.admit), stating its declared origin, its license conditions and the digest of the package's manifest. The owner commits it as a new knowledge source with its own id and returns that exact manifest and a provenance whose origin is added_external_package naming the same origin and conditions, acquired now and not_accepted. The person registers the imported source's own package_published home, apart from the repository source's home. A question over both revisions in the default order (knowledge.question.ask) prefers the repository member and keeps the imported member retained beside it with its own evidence. Nothing is adopted or accepted for any Team, and the import ranks above no existing layer: its provenance has no priority field and the view places it below the repository layer.",
 "spec_sha256": "b10ea36369a9e54e86b8a1348a6c3faf84e273180a92b6476ec5b278401f3d1d",
